/**
\fn pdg::Sprite::addAnimationIK(object config, int order)
\brief Register a two-bone inverse-kinematics controller.

Validates a trial solve before registration. The controller runs in animationStage_Constraint on each evaluation, using the freshly sampled joint offsets. Inspect its result to distinguish unreachable, limited, and stretched solutions.

\param config Configuration object described below.
\param order Signed integer ordering within the constraint stage; default 0.

\return A modifier ID usable with setAnimationIKTarget(), getAnimationIKResult(), and removeAnimationModifier().

\note Call enableAnimationPose() successfully before using this method. The example assumes the rig has a contiguous shoulder/forearm/hand chain.

\par Example
\code{.js}
const ikId = sprite.addAnimationIK({
    root: 'shoulder', middle: 'forearm', tip: 'hand',
    targetX: 12, targetY: 8, space: pdg.animationSpace_Rig
});
sprite.setAnimationIKTarget(ikId, 14, 6, pdg.animationSpace_Rig);
\endcode

\htmlonly[block]
<div class="shared-api-options">
\endhtmlonly

\anchor animation_ik_options
\par Two-bone IK configuration
| Field | Default | Meaning |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `root`, `middle`, `tip` | Required | Bone names or IDs forming a contiguous parent-child-child chain. |
| `targetX`, `targetY` | 0 | Finite target position in the selected space. |
| `space` | animationSpace_Rig | Local uses the root bone's parent frame; World uses the owning layer. |
| `rootLength`, `middleLength` | 0 | Zero derives length from the rig or child offset. Explicit positive lengths must match the joint offsets. Display widths are ignored. |
| `influence` | 1 | Finite blend weight from 0 to 1. |
| `bendDirection` | 1 | Integer +1 or -1 selecting the elbow side. |
| `stretch` | animationIK_NoStretch | Use animationIK_Stretch to allow extending toward out-of-reach targets. |
| `matchOrientation` | false | Whether to aim the tip rotation as well as its position. |
| `targetRotation` | 0 | Finite clockwise target angle in radians. |
| `rootMin`, `middleMin` | -Math.PI | Minimum local joint angles in radians. |
| `rootMax`, `middleMax` | Math.PI | Maximum local joint angles in radians. |

Nonuniform scales and reflections are supported when effective scales are nonsingular. Zero-length segments, incompatible offsets, invalid limits, and singular transforms are rejected atomically.

\htmlonly[block]
</div>
\endhtmlonly

\see setAnimationIKTarget(), getAnimationIKResult(), removeAnimationModifier()
*/
